<!--
  ============================================================================
  Scenario_Utinni.xml                        Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  The campaign's opening narration. `ScenPart_GameStartDialog` is the only place
  it can live: nothing else in the game shows the player a block of text before
  the first tick.

  🔴 THE SCENE IS THE OWNER'S, 2026-08-22, and it is quoted here rather than
  paraphrased because everything below is built on it:

      "the Jawa have just snuck aboard the ancient vessel with a carefully
      imprinted Jawa mind upon a truly ancient persona core, installed it... and
      suddenly the ship is powering up engines and systems thought long since
      dead and loudly announcing its pre-flight sequence. All of this in a Hutt
      junkyard, and the squeals of angry Gamorreans can already be heard running
      to investigate. Time to get out of here!"

  EVERY PROPER NOUN BELOW IS CANON, NOT INVENTED
  ==============================================
    `Kolyska` ("Cradle")   the hull's original name. The Jawa rename it
                           `The Utinni` on taking it, and the Cradle-Mind has
                           never accepted the rename - SCENARIO_SPEC.md, owner
                           2026-08-15. That refusal is the last line's joke.
    Ohm the All-Current    the persona core was patterned off a JAWA mind so it
                           would obey Jawa commands, and inherited that mind's
                           cosmology whole - so it has concluded it IS the god
                           of the living machine. divine_satiation_engine.md.
    the Rakata             the ancients are Rakatan, ruled by the owner and
                           specced in ANCIENTS_AS_RAKATA_SPEC.md.
    Ash'karr, the Sundered ⭐ REQUIRED. SCENARIO_SPEC.md:330 - "The translation
                           'The Sundered' should appear in player-facing text at
                           least once, or the meaning never reaches the player.
                           GameStartDialog is the obvious place." This is the
                           discharge of that requirement.
    the Second Hand        the clan's own faith. "Nothing is ever truly lost -
                           only owed, only mislaid, only waiting for a better
                           master" is lifted from the ideoligion description in
                           JawaTribes.xml, deliberately, so the opening and the
                           religion speak with one voice.

  ⚠️ NO DURATION, NO DATE AND NO DISTANCE IS ASSERTED. A first draft had "nine
  days" and "twenty thousand years"; neither is in any founding doc, and an
  invented number in the opening narration is the kind of thing that later gets
  quoted back as canon. Where the fiction needed a span it uses a comparison
  instead.

  ⭐ ONE PART, AND THAT IS THE FINISHED ANSWER - NOT A GAP
  =======================================================
  The part list once wanted a second ScenPart, `ScenPart_DisableIncident`, to
  stop the storyteller drawing the free-colonist events: `WandererJoin`,
  `RefugeePodCrash`, `WildManWandersIn`. BUILD recommended banning at least
  `WandererJoin`, on the anti-exponential pillar and on "every colonist is a
  Jawa".

  🔴 THE OWNER OVERRULED THAT, 2026-08-22, and the reason is better than the
  recommendation was:

      "keep them in, it allows the Jawa to show that even in those situations,
      they will be compelled to enslave the individual. If it's a Jawa after
      all, then there can be the dynamic of whether anyone falls in love with
      them or not to consider tribal acceptance."

  ⇒ A stranger arriving is not a free colonist in this campaign. It is a
  SITUATION: the clan's own doctrine says what to do with an outsider, and doing
  it in front of the player is characterisation the storyteller hands us for
  nothing. And when the stranger IS a Jawa, the question stops being mechanical
  and becomes social - whether the colony takes them in turns on whether anyone
  forms a bond, which is the tribe deciding its own membership.

  ⛔ SO DO NOT ADD `ScenPart_DisableIncident` LATER "to finish the def". It was
  considered and declined on the fiction, not forgotten. This ScenarioDef is
  COMPLETE at one part.
  ⚠️ And the wider test still holds: a ScenPart earns its place only when it
  expresses something no def, biome, weather or difficulty setting can. Banning
  an incident nobody wanted banned expresses nothing.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ScenarioDef>
    <defName>Jawa_UtinniStart</defName>
    <label>the opened hull</label>
    <description>A clan of Jawa scavengers has woken something in a Hutt junkyard, and it is announcing itself at volume. Start aboard a gravship you do not own, with a machine that thinks it is a god and a yard full of Gamorreans who have just noticed.</description>
    <scenario>
      <summary>Wake the dead ship. Leave before the owners arrive.</summary>
      <parts>
        <li Class="ScenPart_GameStartDialog">
          <def>GameStartDialog</def>
          <text>Nothing is ever truly lost. Only owed, only mislaid, only waiting for a better master.\n\nThe Hutts keep a mountain of the galaxy's discards out here, and this was the oldest thing in it: a Rakatan hull too dead to be worth cutting up, squatting in the sand since before the Cartel had a name for the sand. You went in through a seam no Gamorrean could ever fit through. You took nothing. You measured.\n\nThen you put a mind in it.\n\nThe core was ancient and it was empty, and the pattern you pressed into it was Jawa - so that it would listen to Jawa, so that it would want what Jawa want. It woke believing itself Ohm the All-Current, the spark that wakes a dead engine, and it may well be right. It answers to Kolyska. It has not once answered to the name you painted on its flank.\n\nIt is also, at this moment, running its pre-flight sequence out loud, in a language nobody on this world has heard since the Infinite Empire fell. Engines thought long dead are turning. Every floodlight in the yard has swung toward the noise.\n\nYou can hear the Gamorreans running.\n\nAsh'karr - the Sundered - is a bad world to be caught on and a worse one to be sold on. The hatch is open. The hull is yours because you woke it, and a thing that could still be made to work was never scrap; it was a sleeping hand, owed its waking.\n\nGet it off the ground.</text>
          <closeSound>GameStartSting</closeSound>
        </li>
      </parts>
    </scenario>
  </ScenarioDef>

</Defs>
